    "lawCode": "Add §71-a, Transp L",
    "lawSection": "Transportation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S2429A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the transportation law, in relation to the erection of certain\ntowers on special parkway lands\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo provide for comment prior to the erection of certain towers on\nlands of special parkways.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThe bill would require the Department of Transportation, prior to\nerecting, causing or permitting to be erected, granting easements or\nlicenses for, or otherwise facilitating the erection of any tower on\nlands of the special parkways, to notify the city, town or village in\nwhich the lands are located and to provide them a minimum thirty day\ncomment period.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nIn cases where the State determines communication towers, including\ncell towers, are to be erected on special parkway lands, it should\nrecognize the traditional role of local governments as purveyors of\nland use policy. Obtaining comment from the applicable local\ngovernment before allowing such permanent and readily observable\ntowers to be erected would ensure that local concerns can be advanced.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n2009/2010 A.4219 referred to transportation A.7442 (2001-02), A.455\n(2003-04), A.1725 (2005-06). A.1107 (2007-2008).\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nUnknown.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
